WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.046 --> 00:00:01.260
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.820
- We always like to finish things up

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:04.860
with something cool and
fun that's trending,

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:05.980
this is "What I'm Liking".

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:06.813
(upbeat guitar music)

00:00:06.813 --> 00:00:08.550
(audience clapping)

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.680
Things can get a little intense in life,

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.480
and we all need some comic relief,

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.370
and that's where our next guest comes in.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.297
His new Netflix special is called,

00:00:16.297 --> 00:00:18.090
"Deon Cole Charleen's Boy"

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:19.560
and it's streaming now.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.510
The entire special is a tribute

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.370
to Deon's late mom, Charleen,

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.170
and we have him on the line right now

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.003
to tell us more;

00:00:26.003 --> 00:00:27.396
What's up Deon?

00:00:27.396 --> 00:00:28.479
(audience cheering)

00:00:28.479 --> 00:00:29.723
- Hey, how you doing?

00:00:30.708 --> 00:00:31.890
- I'm so good,

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.150
but I'm sad you're not here in person;

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:33.983
I always love when you come.

00:00:33.983 --> 00:00:35.310
You make me so happy, man.

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:36.300
You're just one of those people,

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.695
you're so infectious.

00:00:38.695 --> 00:00:40.203
(Deon laughing)

00:00:40.203 --> 00:00:41.315
- I wish I could be there.

00:00:41.315 --> 00:00:43.053
I'm down here in Atlanta shooting

00:00:43.053 --> 00:00:45.750
this new show called
"Average Joe", man so-

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.010
- [Kelly] Ah.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:48.990
- We doing what we do, you know?

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:49.980
- Absolutely, absolutely.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:50.820
Well, it's great to see you,

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:53.280
and I'm so sorry for your loss.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.113
This is actually...

00:00:54.113 --> 00:00:54.946
You filmed this

00:00:54.946 --> 00:00:56.340
is it one year to the day

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.930
after you lost your mom?

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:02.010
- Yeah, so my mom had passed
on September 10th, 2021,

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.290
and I had...

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:05.437
Netflix was like,

00:01:05.437 --> 00:01:07.680
"Yo, we want you to shoot a special",

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.330
but I had toured everywhere already.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.400
The only place I didn't tour was New York,

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.320
and I was like, "Yeah,
we'll find out the date",

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.630
and I knew my mom had passed on.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.310
This was her first year anniversary,

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.810
which would've been September 10th,

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:19.920
and I didn't want to work

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:20.940
nowhere around that date,

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:23.910
so I made sure that I
told them to find a place

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:25.950
towards the end of September,

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:27.577
and they just came across me like,

00:01:27.577 --> 00:01:30.000
"Man, don't mourn her, celebrate her,"

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.910
like, "Let her live forever
through what you do.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:34.830
That's how when we lose people,

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.360
they live through us",

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.190
and so I was like, "Man, you know what?

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:39.210
I'm just going to shoot it

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:41.460
on that day that she passed,

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.500
and call it "Charleen's Boy",

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.330
because it'll be a double entendre."

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.820
It'll be who I am,

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:49.380
and it'll be the name of the special,

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:50.437
so when people say,

00:01:50.437 --> 00:01:51.960
"Have you seen "Charleen's Boy?"

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.330
It'll be basically speaking about her,

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.850
and so I shot that whole special

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.590
without the audience even knowing

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:01.020
that this was the anniversary
of her first death,

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.670
and so when I told them at the end,

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:04.530
it resonated with a lot of people and-

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:05.638
- Absolutely.

00:02:05.638 --> 00:02:07.867
- And I just tried to tell everybody like,

00:02:07.867 --> 00:02:10.140
"Yeah, you just never know

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:11.850
what a person is going through,

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:13.770
and embrace those that have lost somebody,

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.210
because they're not the same,

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:16.290
and quit treating them the same,

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:17.730
'cause they're not."

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:19.650
- Thank you so much, Deon.

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:21.270
You're literally one

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:23.130
of my favorite guests that comes here,

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:25.650
and it's because whatever
you are going through,

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:26.940
you're so honest about it,

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.830
and that is so healing,

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:29.663
probably for you,

00:02:29.663 --> 00:02:30.630
but also all those people,

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:31.680
you're saying that watch this,

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:33.060
and it healed them as well,

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.010
and they connected in a different way.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:36.390
Had you not been so open,

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:37.770
that might not have happened,

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:38.850
and you know, you probably reached

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:40.650
so many people that needed that.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:41.483
- Kelly, thank you so much

00:02:41.483 --> 00:02:44.310
for sharing your platform
with so many people.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:46.470
You are such a blessing to everybody,

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:47.613
and I want to thank you

00:02:47.613 --> 00:02:49.920
from the bottom of my
heart as well, definitely.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:50.753
- Thank you.

00:02:50.753 --> 00:02:53.310
It's literally like my favorite thing.

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:54.430
I always say it's like

00:02:55.304 --> 00:02:56.730
the dream job I never knew I wanted,

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.200
and thank you, Deon.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.130
We love you so much.

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:00.150
I can't wait to see you.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:01.170
Come promote

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:03.240
whatever you're working
on right now in person,

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.073
'cause I miss you.

00:03:04.073 --> 00:03:04.906
Okay.

00:03:04.906 --> 00:03:06.330
I'm liking your post right now.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.163
- [Deon] Alright, thank you.

00:03:07.163 --> 00:03:07.996
(Kelly and audience clapping)

00:03:07.996 --> 00:03:08.850
(heart dinging)

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:10.859
Thank you so much, love you.

00:03:10.859 --> 00:03:12.270
- Oh man.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:13.920
I love him so much.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:14.820
He's so cool.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:15.877
Everybody be sure to watch

00:03:15.877 --> 00:03:17.280
"Deon Cole Charleen's Boy",

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.140
streaming now on Netflix.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:20.790
So here's the thing:

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:22.320
we've hit the time in the show

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.420
when we usually give our guest $1,000,

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:25.710
thanks to our season-long partner,

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.540
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.250
the go-to pen of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show",

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.410
but come on, Deon's doing all right.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:32.430
He's got food in his pantry.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:33.263
He's all right.

00:03:33.263 --> 00:03:34.319
He doesn't need the $1,000 so

00:03:34.319 --> 00:03:35.152
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:35.152 --> 00:03:36.660
we thought we're going to give it

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:37.830
to someone in the audience.

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:38.707
How does that sound?

00:03:38.707 --> 00:03:39.540
(audience cheering)

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:40.914
Anybody want it?

00:03:40.914 --> 00:03:42.270
Alright.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:43.394
Well, look under your chairs,

00:03:43.394 --> 00:03:44.227
(suspenseful music)

00:03:44.227 --> 00:03:45.480
'cause someone in this audience

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:46.807
has a $1,000 check taped under it.

00:03:46.807 --> 00:03:47.852
(drumming music)

00:03:47.852 --> 00:03:50.852
(audience chatting)

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:52.808
(upbeat rock music)

00:03:52.808 --> 00:03:54.141
Oh.

00:03:54.141 --> 00:03:56.041
(Kelly clapping)

00:03:56.041 --> 00:03:57.191
Stand up.

00:03:57.191 --> 00:03:58.024
(audience clapping)

00:03:58.024 --> 00:03:59.730
Stand up.
What's your name?

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.410
- Kara.
- [Kelly] Your name is Kara?

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:02.376
- Yeah.

00:04:02.376 --> 00:04:03.840
- First of all, you have
bouncy commercial hair.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.010
It's great.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:05.880
Let's lead with that, Kara.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.520
So what do you think
you'll do with the money?

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:09.960
- Maybe go on a trip, I don't know.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:11.070
- I love it.

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:13.020
Everybody usually says pay bills.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:13.950
Yes, Kara.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:14.783
- I could probably do that.

00:04:14.783 --> 00:04:15.616
- Have fun with it.

00:04:15.616 --> 00:04:16.830
(Kelly laughing and clapping)

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.270
Well, thank you, Kara, for being here.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:19.410
Have so much fun with that money,

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.628
and thank you to all our guests this hour:

00:04:21.628 --> 00:04:23.970
Andie MacDowell, Whitney
Peak, Brad Meltzer,

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:25.710
Scarlett Johansson, Lawrence Aaron.

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:27.090
Y'all have a great day,

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:29.173
and if it's not, well, try and change it.

